+## JSON Merge Patch
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a JSON Merge Patch ([RFC 7386](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)) to a
+JSON document, and returns the merged document as a new value: neither the target nor the patch is mutated. An object
+patch merges member by member, and a member whose value is `null` removes the member from the target. Any other patch
+value (an array, a string, a number, a boolean, or `null` at the top level) replaces the target as a whole. It throws an
+error when the target or the patch is not a JSON value.
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyMergePatch({ name: "ada", tags: ["a"], email: "x@example.com" }, { email: null, tags: ["b"] });
+// { name: "ada", tags: ["b"] }
+```
+
+Merge Patch cannot set a member to `null`: a `null` in a patch always removes the member. Use JSON Patch when a `null`
+value is needed.
+
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
